Upstream:      matrix-authentication-service
               (github.com/element-hq/matrix-authentication-service):
               policies/client_registration/client_registration.rego
Upstreamable:  not as written (it removes confidential clients for everyone).
               A policy.data.client_registration flag with the same effect
               would be.
How:           An issue on element-hq/matrix-authentication-service asking for
               a data flag that limits dynamic registration to public clients,
               or for jwks_uri to be checked like the other client URIs.
Written:       2026-11-23, against matrix-authentication-service 1.29.0
Last checked:  2026-11-23: 1.29.0 (the version in nixpkgs) has no rule on
               token_endpoint_auth_method, jwks or jwks_uri; main not checked
Remove when:   MAS can refuse confidential clients, or attacker-chosen
               jwks_uri, through its config
Applied by:    packages/matrix-authentication-service/outputs.nix (the build
               fails if the patch stops applying)

Dynamic client registration (POST /oauth2/registration) needs no
authentication, and MAS has no setting to turn it off. A client registered
with token_endpoint_auth_method private_key_jwt and a jwks_uri makes MAS GET
that URL from its pod when the client presents a client_assertion at
/oauth2/token: a blind SSRF for anyone who can reach MAS, which is the whole
internet here. Any confidential client can also mint a client_credentials
token and call introspection.

The patch refuses every registration that is not a public client
(token_endpoint_auth_method none, which a registration must state), and any
that carries jwks or jwks_uri. The Matrix clients (Element, Element X) register
as public clients. The policy runs only at registration, so clients registered
before it stay as they are until deleted from the database.

Upstream's policy tests (make -C policies test) register clients without an
auth method and fail with this patch; the package build does not run them.

--- a/policies/client_registration/client_registration.rego
+++ b/policies/client_registration/client_registration.rego
@@ -188,6 +188,18 @@
 	is_public_client
 }
 
+violation contains {"msg": "only public clients (token_endpoint_auth_method none) may register"} if {
+	not is_public_client
+}
+
+violation contains {"msg": "jwks_uri is not allowed"} if {
+	input.client_metadata.jwks_uri
+}
+
+violation contains {"msg": "jwks is not allowed"} if {
+	input.client_metadata.jwks
+}
+
 violation contains {"msg": "missing redirect_uris"} if {
 	requires_redirect_uris
 	not input.client_metadata.redirect_uris
